  specNotes={[
    "Why 24V: a 24V system is two 12V batteries in series, doubling voltage so the same cranking power flows at half the current. Lower current means thinner, lighter wiring and less voltage drop — the reason heavy trucks, buses and semi trailers standardized on 24V.",
    "Matched pairs: the two batteries in a series pair must be identical in model, age and rating. If one is weaker, the pair charges unevenly and both fail early. Always replace a 24V pair together, with two identical batteries.",
    "Charging: use a charger rated for 24V, or charge each 12V battery individually. A 12V charger applied across a 24V series pair will not bring it to a full charge."
